{#
  /menu/vegan-ramen/. Brief: SITE_ARCHITECTURE.md.

  The only dish page that earns itself: 588 vegan queries and 16,186
  impressions producing only 131 clicks, because Tajima sits on page two.
  Real demand, real authority, and the spinach noodle turns a dietary query
  into a craft answer.

  HARD CONSTRAINT FROM THE BRIEF: "the vegan credibility predates the pivot.
  Do not frame it as new." The 2017 runner-up is eight years old. Nothing here
  presents the vegan bowl as a recent addition or as a response to anything.

  The dish, its ingredients, and its price come from menu.json. Nothing about
  this bowl is written here.

  BRIEF SECTION 4 IS NOT BUILT. "Where to get it. Locations from menu.json
  `locations` column." That column is empty on every row (Open Decision #12),
  and two locations genuinely run reduced menus (College Heights is a
  pared-down ramen bar, Plaza Bonita is quick-serve). Naming rooms that serve
  this bowl without the data would send a vegan diner somewhere that may not
  have it, which is worse than sending them to the locations index. Section 4
  routes to /locations/ instead and says the menu varies.
#}
{%- set dish = (menu.items | where("id", "vegan")) | first %}

